    "body": "## Summary\n\n**ADR-075 — Vector 2022 mobile menu layout at narrow viewport (Proposed, diagnosis only).**\n\nFresh trace with permanent `pos=` and `ABS_PUSH` trace extensions reveals the Wikipedia History-too-low issue at narrow viewports (984px content width) is a **Vector 2022 cascade + layout coordination bug**, not just float positioning as ADR-074 hypothesized.\n\n## Four findings from the trace\n\n**A1. Cascade is not applying `position: sticky` to Vector 2022 header elements.**\nAll header elements report `pos=static`. Vector 2022 CSS declares `position: sticky` on `.mw-header` and related elements. Firefox shows a working sticky header at 984px; HoneyBee cascades `static`. Cause likely: unsupported selectors (`:where()`, `:is()`, `@supports`, CSS custom properties).\n\n**A2. Menu children get invalid in-flow geometry.**\n```\nmw-navigation (parent)    x=24, y=217.9, w=976,  h=0\np-navigation (child)      x=16, y=69.0,  w=0,    h=300.4\nvector-main-menu (child)  x=16, y=16.0,  w=0,    h=718.8\n```\nChildren are 8px LEFT of parent and 148px ABOVE parent. Impossible for `pos=static` in-flow children.\n\n**A3. Menu elements laid out 12+ times each.**\nOnce per `vector-dropdown-content` `ABS_PUSH`. Performance cost and geometry-doubling risk.\n\n**A4. 358px gap between `mw-navigation` (h=0) and `mw-content-text` (y=575.9) unexplained by `mw-navigation` alone.**\n\n## The cascade vs layout split\n\nTwo paths needed next session:\n\n**Path A (first):** Firefox DevTools vs HoneyBee `ComputedStyleMap` comparison on 6 header elements. Compare `position`, `display`, `width`, `height`, `float` between browsers.\n\n**Path B (after A):** If cascade values match but geometry is wrong, layout fix — likely the same coordinate-space bug class as ADR-071's inline routing.\n\n**Scope split for next session:**\n- ADR-076 candidate: cascade support for `:where()`, `:is()`, `@supports`, CSS vars\n- ADR-077 candidate: layout coordinate space for absolute-dropdown content\n\n## Permanent traces added (per ADR-073)\n\n- `pos=<static|relative|absolute|fixed|sticky>` appended to every `layout_element: EXIT` trace\n- `ABS_PUSH <tag> id='...' class='...'` on every `pending_absolutes` push\n\nBoth guarded with `log_enabled(LogCategory::LayoutDetail, LogLevel::Trace)`. Zero cost when `HONEYBEE_LOG` unset. Existing `FLOAT` and `NARROW` traces (ADR-074) stay in place.\n\n## What this PR does NOT do\n\n- Does not fix the cascade bug (deferred to ADR-076)\n- Does not fix the layout coordinate bug (deferred to ADR-077)\n- Does not change any behavior\n\n## Test count\n\n694 / 2646 unchanged (diagnosis + traces only, no behavior change).\n\n## Verification category\n\n**Diagnostic + trace addition.** No behavior change.\n\nRefs #282\n",
